        "predicate": "summary",
        "object": "<p>Ian Tyler, already in role on an interim basis, is tasked with shifting strategy to refocus on fossil fuel extraction</p><p>BP has appointed a new chair after a months-long search triggered by the controversial <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/may/26/bp-chair-albert-manifold-ian-tyler\">ousting of Albert Manifold</a>, seeking to draw a line under years of boardroom turmoil at the UK oil and gas company.</p><p>Ian Tyler, who has served as the interim chair and has sat on the BP board as a non-executive director since April 2025, will assume the role on a permanent basis immediately.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/sep/02/bp-appoints-new-chair-after-ousting-of-albert-manifold-in-may\">Continue reading...</a>"
